      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. I'll improve the test by:\n1. Removing all unused imports\n2. Inlining the single-use `doTestFileWithSpecifiedLines` helper into the test method to eliminate unnecessary indirection\n3. Removing the unused `createLinesFile` overload (no-encoding variant)\n4. Adding a named constant for the line count\n5. Using clearer variable names and structured commentsThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version eliminates unnecessary indirection by inlining the single-use `doTestFileWithSpecifiedLines` helper, removes all unused imports and the unused `createLinesFile` overload, introduces a `LINE_COUNT` constant, and adds clear structured comments and more descriptive variable/assertion messages — all without changing the runtime behaviour."
